  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds; business-type (Water, Sewer, Trash) on accrual basis (Statement of Activities shows business-type activities on accrual basis), so business_type uses the proprietary statement (net position, p7); proprietary cash flows (pp8-9) left null as in FY2023/FY2024. Business-type disbursements total = Statement of Activities total business-type expenses 143,950 (p2) = operating 133,514 + interest 9,636 + bond fees 800; receipts computed from operating revenues + nonoperating interest and grant income. Business-type 'Other revenue' 1,659 kept in charges for services: Statement of Activities Water charges for services 85,174 (p2) = Sales 83,515 + Other revenue 1,659. Grant income 22,035 (Water, nonoperating; capital grants in the Statement of Activities) has no grantor printed: category other, detail Grants. Governmental receipts/disbursements from Total Governmental Funds column (p5); transfers from fund columns (General in 40,000, Sales Tax out 40,000; Total column nets to zero). Governmental cash: Balance Sheet p4 Cash and cash equivalents 293,644; CDs 13,408 (ending_investments) and County treasurer cash 1,573 printed separately (not added to ending_cash); beginning cash not printed. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), since it includes capital assets. General Fund detail from the departmental combining statement (p13, more detailed than the p10 budget schedule, which is not recorded to avoid double counting). Street and Sales Tax Fund from their budget schedules (pp11-12). No business-type detail (as FY2023/FY2024). Read pages 1-13 of 13"
